course: dictionary
lesson: 1332
title: Calve: birth and breaking away
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Calve is a verb, a doing word. It has two meanings, so the words around it tell you which one is meant. Check the clues: is the subject an animal or a huge block of ice?
explain: For cows and some other animals, calve means to give birth to a calf. «Dairy cows usually calve about once a year.» The cow is the one having a baby, so calve means to give birth.
explain: For glaciers and icebergs, calve means a big piece of ice breaks off and falls into the sea. Look for clues such as ice, sea or iceberg, which show that the word is about the ice, not a baby.
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence. If «the glacier calved» makes sense as «the glacier had a big piece of ice break off», you have found the right meaning.
fact: Calve is a verb. Its forms are calve, calves, calved and calving.
fact: «Calve» means to give birth to a calf. It is used for cows, whales, elephants and some other animals.
fact: A calf is a baby cow, or the baby of some other large animal, such as a whale or an elephant.
fact: «Calve» can also mean that a big piece of ice breaks off a glacier or iceberg and falls into the sea.
fact: Glaciers calve in cold places such as Antarctica, Greenland and Alaska.
exercise: «Dairy cows usually calve about once a year.» What does calve mean here? | To eat grass in a field | To give milk to people | *To give birth to a calf | To sleep in the barn
exercise: «The glacier began to calve, and a huge chunk of ice fell into the sea.» What does calve mean here? | To grow taller each winter | To melt slowly in the sun | To make loud music | *To have a big piece of ice break off and fall into the sea
exercise: Which word is the name for a baby cow? | *calf | calving | calve | calved
test:
«Last spring, our cow calved twins, and both calves are healthy.» Which word means the same as calved here? | Gave birth to | *Gave birth to (two babies), so calved means to give birth | Ate | Moved to a new farm
test:
Last spring, our cow ___ twin calves. Choose the right form of calve. | calves | calving | *calved | calf
exam:
«Last year a huge piece of the glacier calved and crashed into the sea.» Which phrase best explains calved? | Grew bigger in the sun | *Broke off and fell into the sea | Had a baby | Turned into water and disappeared
